==Trivia==
*This stage's name was changed from ''At last, I'm a Cat'' to ''At Least I'm a Cat'' in [[Version 6.7 Update|Version 6.7]]. Note that when [[Weak & Mildly Acidic]] was first released, the sub-chapter info screen already listed it as ''At least I'm a Cat'' (with a lowercase "L"), so ''At last, I'm a Cat'' was likely just a typo that went unnoticed for some time.
*At Least I'm a Cat's Japanese name, At Least, Be a Cat (せめて、ネコらしく), could be a reference to "At Least, Be Human" (せめて、人間らしく), the Japanese title of ''[[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Neon Genesis Evangelion]]'' [https://wiki.evageeks.org/Episode_22 episode 22]. The episode depicts [[Asuka Langley (Super Rare Cat)|Asuka]]'s declining mental state and traumatic childhood, which the mind-bending 15th Angel, Arael, forces her to relive; overall, it fits right in with the psychological themes of [[Body & Soul]] and [[Weak & Mildly Acidic]].

